2. Release Notes 

 Version 1.0 — Student Tracker Application 
 
Release Date: November 2025 
 
This release represents the first full deployment of the Student Tracker Application, implementing all core features required for class check-in/out, attendance monitoring, messaging, and role-based system access. 
 
New Features 
- Chat/Messaging System 
- Enables real-time messaging between students and instructors, with support for group-chats and persistent message storage. 
 
Check-In/Check-Out System 
- Students can check in to a single class at a time. The system records check-in/out timestamps and geolocation (longitude/latitude) for verification. 
 
Attendance Tracking 
- Automatically logs and stores attendance records linked to each student’s ID, including check-in data and location. 
 
Geolocation Integration 
- Integrated with Abstract’s IP Geolocation API to validate user location on check-in and check-out. 
 
Class Roster & Enrollment View 
- Instructors can access class rosters, see student details, and open chat sessions directly from the roster view. 
 
Login/Logout & Authentication 
- Secure user login with role-based access for Students, Instructors, and Admins. 
 
Navigation Menu 
- Updated UI navigation menu to provide easy access to messaging, attendance, and class features. 

 

Improvements 
- UI refinements for easier navigation. 
 
-More consistent handling of user roles and permissions. 
 
- Enhanced backend structure for message persistence and storing geolocation records. 
 
Bug Fixes 
- Fixed issue causing duplicate chats to appear in the database. 
 
- Corrected table header formatting in the instructor and admin views. 
 
- Resolved inconsistent username display within chat interfaces. 
 
Known Limitations 
- Students may only check in to one class at a time. 
 
- Geolocation accuracy may vary depending on IP detection limitations. 